Z||000004||maryjane||10-26-2001||01:19 AM||||Can't stand any of the store bought stuff.<BR>1/2 head of shredded cabbage(or cole slaw mix)<BR>2lbs of browned ground beef<BR>1-1/2 cups of uncooked rice<BR>2 cans diced Rotel brand tomatos and chili's<P>Mix it all up together in a rice cooker, barely cover with water. (& I mean just barely).<BR>Turn on the rice cooker and when the bell rings, it's done. umm-umm-good.<BR>or:<BR>1- 6 oz pkg of cornbread mix (Mexican style if you wish)<BR>1 egg<BR>2/3 cup of milk<BR>1 can ea of creme corn and whole kernel corn(16 oz) drain the whole kernel corn<BR>8 oz of sour creme<BR>1 cup grated cheddar cheese<BR>1/2 cup chopped onion,1/3 cup chopped bell pepper, sauteed in butter.<BR>Mix it all together & bake at 350* for 35-40 mins or till cornbread is done in a 9x13 greased casserole dish. Try it you'll like it. Much better than the chicken fried bacon.<BR>Yes, I do all the cooking at our house, since Jane has been ill. Sorry for hijackin your thread. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Don||||reg||1
